        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 229,
        "headingText": "<p>8810/0 Desmoplastic fibroblastoma</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-31T09:23:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 397,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 230,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58271,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 230,
        "headingText": "<p>EE6Y &amp; XH2ZF3 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Desmoplastic fibroblastoma</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-23T16:14:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 398,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 231,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58272,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> collagenous fibroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58273,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58274,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common sites are the upper arm, shoulder, lower limb, back, forearm, hand, and foot {7661281; 8832562; 9670823}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58275,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour typically presents as an asymptomatic, slow-growing subcutaneous mass, but fascial and skeletal muscle involvement is relatively common.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58276,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoplastic fibroblastoma is a rare tumour that predominantly affects adults, with a median age of 50&ndash;60&nbsp;years.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58277,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58278,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "<p>Most of the karyotypic studies of desmoplastic fibroblastoma have demonstrated a recurrent t(2;11)(q31;q12) {15036892; 22137488; 17894801}. Deregulated expression of FOSL1 appears to be the functional outcome of 11q12 rearrangements in desmoplastic fibroblastoma, based on global gene expression profiling and quantitative real-time PCR {22411068}. Notably, diffuse, strong FOSL1 nuclear immunoreactivity is seen in desmoplastic fibroblastomas with 11q12 rearrangement, in contrast to the absence of overexpression in 11q12-rearranged fibromas of tendon sheath {27442992}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-14T14:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58279,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoplastic fibroblastomas are usually relatively small, often measuring 1&ndash;4&nbsp;cm in greatest dimension, but examples &gt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;cm and as large as 20&nbsp;cm have occurred. Grossly, the lesions appear well circumscribed and form oval, fusiform, or discoid masses. Some examples have an externally lobulated, cobblestone-like surface. The tumours have a firm, cartilage-like consistency, and on cut section they have a homogeneous pearl-grey colour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58280,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although often well demarcated grossly, most tumours microscopically infiltrate into subcutaneous fat, and approximately 25% extend into skeletal muscle {7661281; 8832562; 9670823}. Rare examples are purely intramuscular. The lesions have abundant collagenous or myxocollagenous matrix with low vascularity. Cellularity ranges from low to moderate, and the neoplastic cells tend to be uniformly distributed within the extracellular matrix. The lesional cells are stellate-shaped, bipolar, and spindled, and they have uniform, bland nuclei with distinct small nucleoli. Mitotic figures are uncommon. Rare examples have focal intravascular growth. The tumour cells may be focally positive for SMA.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58281,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 240,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58282,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 240,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 410,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 243,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58283,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 243,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> hypocellular with abundant collagenous or myxocollagenous matrix; stellate, bipolar, and spindle cells with small nucleoli.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 408,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 241,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58284,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 241,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 409,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 242,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58285,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 242,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The behaviour of this tumour is benign, and none of the published clinicopathological series have documented any recurrences.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:17:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
